                <pb facs="0708" n="596" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg596"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 23814/11.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Ambassador Reid.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic">March 30,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1261.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The department has received your No. 1216
                    of the 18th instant, in regard to the anticipated emigration to the United
                    States of the British subject Alfred Lumb, a confessed counterfeiter.</p>
                <p>The department approves your note to the foreign office on the subject.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>(For <signed>Mr. Knox</signed>.)<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Huntington Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
